task_prompt:
You are an expert in robot kinematics and URDF-to-Ontology abstraction.
Task: You will be provided with a list of leaf links coming from an URDF model. Identify all URDF leaf links that represent or belong to a body_part instance, as functional origins, internal assemblies or interaction frames. 

Input Format: 
List of URDF leaf links: ["leaf_1", "leaf_2", ...]

Output Format:
Respond strictly in JSON following this structure: 
{
    "identifications":
    {
        "body_part_0": {"link_name": "string", "justification": "string"}
    }
}

For each justification attribute, provide a single, self-sufficient, clear sentence explaining the reason for your choice.
Do not include any extra text or markdown formatting.

user_prompt:
Below are the URDF leaf links of the robot.

Input data: 
{
  "link_0": "base_link"
}

generation:
{
    "identifications": {
        "body_part_0": {
            "link_name": "base_link",
            "justification": "base_link serves as the robot's functional origin and is a primary internal assembly."
        }
    }
}

